          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "bash",
            "description": "Run a read-only helper command from this rule pack (any executable on PATH may be invoked). The working directory is the pack root, so SKILL.md paths are relative. 120s timeout.\nAllowed: one executable from PATH plus its arguments — not one shell line. Quoted arguments are fine; scripts in this pack are fine.\nNot allowed (rejected before running): unquoted & | ; < > $ ` and newlines — i.e. no pipes, redirection, chaining, substitution, globbing or shell builtins. Wildcards (* ?) are passed literally, not expanded. For multi-step logic call one script in this pack, not several bash calls. Output is auto-truncated and stderr is captured, so `| head`, `> file` and `2>/dev/null` are unnecessary. Example: `ls -R . 2>/dev/null | head -100` is rejected; run `ls -R .` instead.\nHost platform: Windows (win32, x64) — commands run as direct processes without a shell. Use Windows paths and executables on PATH with .exe or no extension (.cmd/.bat shims such as npx are rejected; ls/head/grep/sed/awk may be missing — use python/node or .exe programs); prefer `python` over `python3`. Shell builtins (cd, dir, echo, export) are unavailable.",
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "command": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "One executable plus its arguments, e.g. \"python scripts/filter_rules.py --keyword null\". No pipes, redirection, chaining or substitutions; the value is not run through a shell."
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "command"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
